",[504,505,507],"h2",{"id":506},"syntax","Syntax",[509,510,511,528,534,556,562],"ul",{},[512,513,514,517,518,517,521,517,524,527],"li",{},[114,515,516],{},"@:key",", ",[114,519,520],{},"@.upper:key",[114,522,523],{},"@.lower:key",[114,525,526],{},"@.capitalize:key"," (first letter only).",[512,529,530,533],{},[114,531,532],{},"@:{'key'}"," for a key a bare link cannot spell.",[512,535,536,537,517,540,544,545,548,549,552,553,365],{},"A bare key runs to whitespace or one of ",[114,538,539],{},"{ } @ % | ( )",[541,542,543],"strong",{},"dots and commas included",": ",[114,546,547],{},"@:brand."," names\n",[114,550,551],{},"brand.",". End a sentence with the quoted form: ",[114,554,555],{},"@:{'brand'}.",[512,557,558,561],{},[114,559,560],{},"{name}"," placeholders of the linked text stay and are filled when the message is read.",[512,563,564,565,568,569,572],{},"Modifiers follow the locale's case rules (Turkish ",[114,566,567],{},"i"," → ",[114,570,571],{},"İ",", and so on).",[504,574,576],{"id":575},"rules","Rules",[509,578,579,589,611,618],{},[512,580,581,582,585,586,588],{},"A link can point to a root key, a page key or a key of a fallback locale. A message read in a locale that falls\nback to English links that locale's words: with ",[114,583,584],{},"\"brand\""," translated, the German ",[114,587,160],{}," shows the German brand.",[512,590,591,592,595,596,599,600,603,604,610],{},"A missing key, a subtree, a cycle or an unknown modifier leaves the ",[541,593,594],{},"whole"," message as written. ",[114,597,598],{},"build()","\ncalls ",[114,601,602],{},"missing"," once for it, and ",[495,605,607],{"href":606},"\u002Fguides\u002Fchecks-and-tracing#check",[114,608,609],{},"check()"," lists it with the reason.",[512,612,613,614,617],{},"Messages added later with ",[114,615,616],{},"add_messages"," are not resolved.",[512,619,620],{},"Files loaded lazily or over the network resolve their links when they load. A link from an eagerly loaded\nfile into a lazy one stays as w